      "carousel": false,
      "figures": 3,
      "text": [
        "Built by lifters, for lifters",
        "Iron Works opened in 2016 in a disused steel unit off Alma Street, and we've kept the bones of the building — exposed brick, girders, and a floor that's seen more chalk than paint. We're not a chain gym. There's no smoothie bar, no tanning beds, and no sales pitch waiting at the door.",
        "What you'll find is proper equipment — power racks, deadlift platforms, and enough plates to go around — plus a small team of coaches who actually know your name and your numbers. Whether you're chasing your first pull-up or your next competition total, this is a gym built around getting stronger, s",
        "Est. in Kelham Island"
      ]
    },
    {
      "top": 1816,
      "height": 1094,
      "kind": "cards",
      "label": "Training that fits how you want to work",
      "cards": 6,
